# Line endings.
#
# build.sh runs on a Linux container. Checked out with CRLF — which is what
# git does by default on a Windows machine with core.autocrlf on — the shebang
# line ends in a carriage return, and the kernel looks for an interpreter
# literally named "bash\r". The error is `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`,
# which does not obviously mean "line endings" to anybody reading it at the
# top of a failed deploy log.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, less catastrophic: these are read by Linux tooling and by
# other people's editors, and a mixed-ending diff hides the real change.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
